# fresh_dev_suspend_mmio_before_did: Between a successful rvg_device_will_resume and rvg_device_did_resume the registers read the blob's values (0x1000 1, 0x101c the root page, 0x1034 the version), though nothing is rebuilt and nothing raises. A root-FIFO doorbell then only stores the written offset, since there is no root FIFO to poke; rvg_device_did_resume rebuilds the FIFO at the blob's offsets and its NOP is not run then (0x100c still reads the old offset); it runs, and its stamp publishes, with the next doorbell.
